.TH SENSOR-W1THERM 1 "January 2026" "sensor-w1therm 1.0" "WildlifeSystems"
.SH NAME
sensor-w1therm \- read w1_therm 1-Wire temperature sensors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sensor-w1therm
[\fB\-\-version\fR|\fB\-v\fR|\fBversion\fR|\fBidentify\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBsetup\fR|\fBenable\fR|\fBmock\fR|\fBinternal\fR|\fBexternal\fR|\fBall\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sensor-w1therm
reads temperature data from w1_therm 1-Wire temperature sensors connected to the system.
The command scans for all supported sensors (DS18S20, DS1822, DS18B20, DS1825, DS28EA00)
on the 1-Wire bus and outputs their readings in JSON format compatible with the
WildlifeSystems sensor-control framework.
.PP
The 1-Wire interface must be enabled in the Raspberry Pi configuration before sensors
can be detected. Use the 'enable' command to configure this automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-v, version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B identify
Returns exit code 60 to identify this sensor type to the WildlifeSystems framework.
.TP
.B list
Lists the measurement types supported by this sensor. Outputs "temperature".
.TP
.B setup
Configures all connected sensors for fast reading by setting conversion time
and resolution. Should be run once after boot (handled automatically by systemd service).
.TP
.B enable
Enables the 1-Wire interface by adding the w1-gpio device tree overlay to
/boot/firmware/config.txt (or /boot/config.txt on older systems). Requires root
privileges. A reboot is required after running this command.
.TP
.B mock
Output mock sensor data for testing without hardware. Returns a fixed value
(21.375\[de]C) useful for testing data pipelines without physical sensors.
.TP
.B internal
Output only readings from sensors marked as internal in the configuration file.
.TP
.B external
Output only readings from sensors marked as external (not internal) in the configuration file.
.TP
.B all
Output all sensor readings (default if no command given).
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
When run without arguments, the command outputs a JSON array containing sensor readings.
Each sensor reading includes:
.PP
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
sensor: The sensor type (e.g., "ds18b20", "ds1822")
.IP \(bu 2
measures: The measurement type ("temperature")
.IP \(bu 2
unit: The unit of measurement ("Celsius")
.IP \(bu 2
value: The temperature reading in degrees Celsius
.IP \(bu 2
sensor_id: The unique 1-Wire device ID (or overridden value from config)
.IP \\(bu 2
sensor_name: (optional) Human-readable name from configuration file
.IP \\(bu 2
internal: (optional) Boolean indicating if sensor is internal, from configuration file
.IP \(bu 2
error: (optional) Error message if reading failed
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Enable 1-Wire interface (first-time setup, requires reboot):
.B sudo sensor-w1therm enable
.TP
Read all connected w1_therm sensors:
.B sensor-w1therm
.TP
List supported measurements:
.B sensor-w1therm list
.TP
Configure sensors for fast reading:
.B sensor-w1therm setup
.TP
Identify sensor type (for sensor-control integration):
.B sensor-w1therm identify
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/*/w1_slave
1-Wire device interface files where temperature readings are obtained.
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/*/temperature
Alternative sysfs entry providing direct temperature reading in millidegrees.
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/w1_bus_master1/therm_bulk_read
Bulk read trigger for optimized multi-sensor reading.
.TP
.I /boot/config.txt
or
.I /boot/firmware/config.txt
Raspberry Pi configuration file where 1-Wire interface is enabled.
.TP
.I /etc/ws/sensors/w1therm.json
Configuration file for sensor settings. This JSON file allows you to override
sensor properties. Each sensor is identified by its hardware ID (hw_id) and can
have the following properties overridden:
.RS
.IP \\(bu 2
hw_id: The 1-Wire hardware ID to match (e.g., "28-00000a1b2c3d")
.IP \\(bu 2
sensor_id: Override the sensor_id in output
.IP \\(bu 2
sensor_name: Human-readable name for the sensor
.IP \\(bu 2
internal: Boolean (true/false) indicating if the sensor is internal
.RE
.PP
Example configuration:
.RS
.nf
[
  {"hw_id": "28-00000a1b2c3d", "sensor_name": "CPU Temperature", "internal": true},
  {"hw_id": "28-00000e4f5g6h", "sensor_id": "outdoor_temp", "sensor_name": "Garden", "internal": false}
]
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 60
Returned when called with 'identify' option
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensor-control (1)
.SH REFERENCES
.TP
